Package: npmatch
Title: A Tiered Workflow for Probabilistic Record Linkage of Organization Data
Version: 0.1.1.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Jesse", "Lecy", email = "jdlecy@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Manages the steps of matching organization records (entity name
    plus variable geographic detail) to a reference database when no shared
    identifier exists: alias enumeration, input standardization, corpus
    pre-preparation (tokenization and inverse document frequency), candidate
    generation by blocking and fuzzy comparison, tiered adjudication, and
    packaging the residual for human or LLM review. Standardization comes from
    'npnormalize' and alias enumeration from 'matchdb'; 'reclin2' supplies
    blocked pairing and comparison. Adds a hard "do-not-match" veto engine,
    geography-adaptive weighting, and tiered (YES / MAYBE / NO) sorting with a
    structured hand-off. Ships wired for federal registrants (SAM) to the IRS
    Business Master File of exempt organizations, which is one deployment of the
    framework rather than a requirement of it.
